<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
      The Android 12+ (API 31) launch splash.

      The platform draws this one itself, before the app gets control, and from
      targetSdk 31 that is mandatory and cannot be turned off. So the job here is
      not to add a splash but to dress the platform's own: the V mark in its icon
      slot, and the name and motto in its branding slot, on our background colour.

      Two rules follow from the platform owning it, and both were learned the hard
      way from a flickering launch:

      1. The icon slot is a fixed 288dp square whose artwork must stay inside an
         inner 192dp circle. A wordmark there is clipped and illegible, which is
         why the name and motto go to windowSplashScreenBrandingImage instead of
         being crammed into the icon.

      2. Whatever sits behind the platform splash must be pixel-identical to it.
         The platform FADES its splash out, so an unmatched image underneath
         reappears as that fade completes: the logo drops to nothing for a frame
         and then snaps back at full strength, which is precisely the flicker
         users reported. MainActivity removes the splash in one cut instead of
         letting it fade, and res/drawable-v31/splash_screen.xml draws the same
         icon at the same geometry, so the handoff changes nothing either way.

         This is not a flat colour, which was the first attempt: Android TV gets
         no platform splash at all, so a flat colour there meant a plain dark
         screen and no logo for the whole bundle load. drawable-television
         supplies the full lock-up for that case.

      The whole style is restated rather than inherited because a resource
      qualifier replaces a style definition, it does not merge into it.
    -->
    <style name="SplashTheme" parent="AppTheme">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/splash_screen</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/background</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBrandingImage">@drawable/splash_branding</item>
    </style>

</resources>
